1
00:00:03,264 --> 00:00:06,006
SHE'S BEEN RUNNING
INTELLIGENCE DOWN IN FRESNO.NEW BOSS?

2
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,833
NEW BOSS.
MADELEINE HIGHTOWER.

3
00:00:07,833 --> 00:00:10,836
CHIEF DEPUTY A.G. SAYS SHE'LL
BE HERE SOMETIME TOMORROW.

4
00:00:10,836 --> 00:00:12,882
WORD IS
SHE'S HARD AS NAILS--

5
00:00:12,882 --> 00:00:15,841
POLITICAL,
TIGHT STATEHOUSE CONNECTIONS.SO THIS IS GOOD FOR US.

6
00:00:15,841 --> 00:00:18,192
WE'LL HAVE
SOME REAL MUSCLE UPSTAIRS.WE'LL SEE.

7
00:00:18,192 --> 00:00:20,194
NO NEED TO BE NERVOUS.

8
00:00:20,194 --> 00:00:21,847
I'M NOT NERVOUS.

9
00:00:21,847 --> 00:00:24,198
YOU'RE AN EXEMPLARY AGENT.
NO REASON FOR BUTTERFLIES.

10
00:00:24,198 --> 00:00:25,851
NO BUTTERFLIES.
I'M FINE.

11
00:00:25,851 --> 00:00:27,723
KEEP TELLING YOURSELF
THAT.

12
00:00:42,390 --> 00:00:43,869
HOW YA DOING?

13
00:00:43,869 --> 00:00:46,133
VIC BANDINO, ALPHA BRAVO
RESIDENTIAL SECURITY.

14
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:48,787
APPRECIATE
YOUR QUICK RESPONSE.AGENT LISBON.
THIS IS PATRICK JANE,

15
00:00:48,787 --> 00:00:51,312
AND THIS IS AG--

16
00:00:51,312 --> 00:00:54,315
WAYNE RIGSBY. CBI, HUH?
YOU DID OKAY. [laughs]HI, BANDINO. WHAT'S UP?
[chuckles]

17
00:00:54,315 --> 00:00:57,318
WE WORKED A COUPLE OF CASES
TOGETHER BACK IN THE DAY.

18
00:00:57,318 --> 00:01:00,930
SAN DIEGO P.D. ARSON SQUAD.[chuckles] YEAH. BOY,
THOSE WERE THE TIMES, HUH?

19
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:03,802
REMEMBER THAT STAKEOUT
IN PISMO?YOU EVER CALL THAT CHICK?

20
00:01:03,802 --> 00:01:05,804
YEAH--WOULD YOU SHOW US
THE BODY, MR. BANDINO?

21
00:01:05,804 --> 00:01:07,980
YES, MA'AM.
YEAH, OF COURSE. PLEASE.

22
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:10,026
HE'S IN THE POOL HOUSE.

23
00:01:10,026 --> 00:01:12,376
NAME'S JAMES SMITHSON--
28, BRITISH CITIZEN.

24
00:01:12,376 --> 00:01:15,423
HE'S A HIGH-PRICED TUTOR
FOR LOCAL KIDS.

25
00:01:15,423 --> 00:01:18,165
DAUGHTER OF THE HOMEOWNER'S
ONE OF THE STUDENTS.

26
00:01:18,165 --> 00:01:20,819
COUPLE MONTHS AGO
THEY LET HIM MOVE IN HERE.

27
00:01:20,819 --> 00:01:24,258
RIGSBY, CAN YOU FIND OUT
WHY THE CORONER'S NOT HERE?[Rigsby] YEAH, SURE.

28
00:01:29,263 --> 00:01:31,308
WHO FOUND THE BODY? YOU?

29
00:01:31,308 --> 00:01:34,355
THE HOMEOWNER'S KID.
SHE WAS COMING IN FOR A LESSON.

30
00:01:34,355 --> 00:01:37,836
[sighs] SHE CALLED HER DAD.
HE CALLED ME. I CALLED YOU.NOT THE LOCAL POLICE?
WHY US EXACTLY?

31
00:01:37,836 --> 00:01:40,100
I DON'T KN--WHAT THE HELL, VIC?

32
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:44,191
YOU WERE SUPPOSED TO CALL ME
THE SECOND THEY GOT HERE.EXCUSE ME, SIR?

33
00:01:44,191 --> 00:01:46,628
I'M HOPPER BANKS.AGENT LISBON, CBI.
THIS IS A CRIME SCENE.

34
00:01:46,628 --> 00:01:48,412
[Hopper] IT'S MY PLACE.

35
00:01:48,412 --> 00:01:52,764
MR. BANKS, I NEED YOU TO LEAVE.
CAN YOU DO THAT FOR ME?

36
00:01:52,764 --> 00:01:56,986
I'LL BE IN THE MAIN HOUSE.
I'LL EXPECT A FULL REPORT.

37
00:02:00,816 --> 00:02:03,210
THAT'S WHY I CALLED YOU.

38
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:05,212
OLD CALIFORNIA MONEY,
LOTS OF CLOUT.

39
00:02:05,212 --> 00:02:08,171
LOCAL P.D. WON'T CUT IT.
HE WANTS THE BEST.

40
00:02:08,171 --> 00:02:10,565
CORONER'S ON HIS WAY.A SINGLE GUNSHOT.

41
00:02:10,565 --> 00:02:13,524
JUDGING BY THE WOUND,
LOOKS LIKE A .38. NO WEAPON.

42
00:02:13,524 --> 00:02:15,526
DON'T WORRY.
IT'S A VISUAL INSPECTION.

43
00:02:15,526 --> 00:02:17,224
DIDN'T TOUCH A THING.

44
00:02:17,224 --> 00:02:19,530
[Lisbon] NO SIGN
OF ASSAULT OR ROBBERY?

45
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:23,012
REAL FANCY RéSUMé,
THIS GUY.

46
00:02:23,012 --> 00:02:25,014
GRADUATED
FROM ETON AND OXFORD.

47
00:02:25,014 --> 00:02:28,409
LAST EMPLOYER WAS SOME
HOTSHOT PREP SCHOOL BACK EAST.

48
00:02:28,409 --> 00:02:31,151
MEH,
I WOULDN'T BE SO SURE.

49
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:32,978
EXCUSE ME?THE FACIAL SCAR.

50
00:02:32,978 --> 00:02:35,981
ETON BOY GETS A CUT ON HIS HEAD,
AND HE NEEDS A PLASTIC SURGEON,

51
00:02:35,981 --> 00:02:38,070
HE GETS A PLASTIC SURGEON.

52
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:40,682
MY GUESS--THE WHOLE RéSUMé
IS A FAIRY TALE.

53
00:02:40,682 --> 00:02:42,988
EXCUSE ME?YOU'RE EXCUSED.

54
00:02:42,988 --> 00:02:47,036
I CHECKED HIM OUT MYSELF.WELL, I'M WRONG THEN.

55
00:02:47,036 --> 00:02:51,083
UH... NO BLISTERS
OR CALLUSES ON HIS HANDS.

56
00:02:51,083 --> 00:02:53,216
A LOT OF DIRT
UNDER HIS FINGERNAILS.

57
00:02:53,216 --> 00:02:56,219
[Vic] WHO IS THIS GUY?[Rigsby] IT'S A LONG STORY.

58
00:02:56,219 --> 00:02:58,178
[sniffs] HMM.[Lisbon] ANYTHING ELSE?

59
00:03:00,049 --> 00:03:02,138
[Vic] I GOT THE CALL
AT 3:35.

60
00:03:02,138 --> 00:03:04,488
I WAS AT
A CLIENT'S RESIDENCE NEARBY,

61
00:03:04,488 --> 00:03:06,447
WORKING AN ALARM UPGRADE.

62
00:03:06,447 --> 00:03:08,927
ARRIVED HERE AT 3:52.

63
00:03:08,927 --> 00:03:12,453
BODY WAS STILL WARM,

64
00:03:12,453 --> 00:03:16,021
SO I GUESS THE TIME OF DEATH WAS
A GOOD HOUR BEFORE THAT.

65
00:03:16,021 --> 00:03:17,458
[gasps]

66
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:19,068
GUESS AGAIN.

67
00:03:36,825 --> 00:03:38,218
[police radio chatter]

68
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:39,828
IT'S CALLED
LAZARUS SYNDROME.

69
00:03:39,828 --> 00:03:41,482
GUY'S HEART SOMEHOW CAUGHT
AN ELECTRICAL CHARGE

70
00:03:41,482 --> 00:03:44,180
AND RESTARTED.
HEY, IT HAPPENS.

71
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:47,792
SO YOU'RE SAYING HE'S ALIVE?WELL, IF YOU CAN CALL THAT
LIVING. HE'S BRAIN-DEAD.

72
00:03:47,792 --> 00:03:50,186
WITH NO OXYGEN
FOR MORE THAN TEN MINUTES,

73
00:03:50,186 --> 00:03:52,188
HE'S NOT COMING BACK.THERE'S SECURITY CAMERAS
OUT THERE.

74
00:03:52,188 --> 00:03:54,190
HAVE BANDINO SHOW YOU
THE FOOTAGE.

75
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:56,845
MAYBE WE'LL GET LUCKY
AND CATCH A LOOK AT THE SHOOTER.

76
00:03:56,845 --> 00:03:59,587
I NEED TO GO
AND TALK TO THE LITTLE GIRL

77
00:03:59,587 --> 00:04:01,676
WHO FOUND THE BODY.YOU GOT IT.

78
00:04:01,676 --> 00:04:05,723
[rustling]

79
00:04:09,161 --> 00:04:11,076
WHAT ARE YOU LOOKING FOR?

80
00:04:11,076 --> 00:04:14,471
THE DIRT UNDER HIS NAILS
SMELLED LIKE ROSEMARY.

81
00:04:16,908 --> 00:04:19,041
YEAH.

82
00:04:19,041 --> 00:04:20,956
YEAH.

83
00:04:28,485 --> 00:04:32,097
WHATEVER WAS INSIDE THIS BOX
KILLED OUR MAN.

84
00:04:32,097 --> 00:04:35,100
WELL, THE CASE IS
PRACTICALLY CLOSED.

85
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:39,104
THERE'S NO REASON TO BE
SNARKY.

86
00:04:39,104 --> 00:04:41,106
IT WAS MY WIFE JOLENE,
REALLY.

87
00:04:41,106 --> 00:04:44,109
SHE SAW HOW MUCH JAMES HELPED
LANIE WITH HER SCHOOLWORK,

88
00:04:44,109 --> 00:04:47,112
AND WHEN SHE HEARD
HE NEEDED A PLACE TO LIVE,

89
00:04:47,112 --> 00:04:49,114
SHE RENTED THE POOL HOUSE
TO HIM.

90
00:04:49,114 --> 00:04:51,073
I GUESS HE'S BEEN HERE,
UH...

91
00:04:51,073 --> 00:04:53,684
I DON'T KNOW.
A COUPLE OF MONTHS, MAYBE.

92
00:04:53,684 --> 00:04:55,686
VERY GENEROUS
OF YOUR WIFE.

93
00:04:55,686 --> 00:04:58,080
JOLENE HAS A BIG HEART.

94
00:04:58,080 --> 00:04:59,777
IS THIS HER?

95
00:04:59,777 --> 00:05:01,170
MY MUSE.

96
00:05:01,170 --> 00:05:02,998
GOOD-LOOKING. MM.

97
00:05:02,998 --> 00:05:06,044
SHE TURNED ME
INTO A REAL ARTIST.

98
00:05:06,044 --> 00:05:08,003
BEFORE I MET HER,
I WAS TAKING SNAPSHOTS.

99
00:05:08,003 --> 00:05:11,659
MR. BANKS, WE'RE GONNA NEED
TO TALK TO YOUR DAUGHTER.

100
00:05:11,659 --> 00:05:14,879
I'M SORRY. LANIE'S TOO UPSET
TO TALK AT THE MOMENT.

101
00:05:14,879 --> 00:05:17,055
PLEASE. MAYBE LATER.

102
00:05:17,055 --> 00:05:20,145
WE NEED TO SPEAK TO HER
WHEN HER MEMORY'S FRESH.SHE SAW WHAT YOU SAW.

103
00:05:20,145 --> 00:05:22,626
SHE CAME HOME,
WENT TO THE POOL HOUSE

104
00:05:22,626 --> 00:05:25,455
FOR SOME HOMEWORK HELP...WE'RE GONNA HAVE
TO HEAR THAT FROM HER.

105
00:05:25,455 --> 00:05:27,762
AND SHE FOUND A DEAD BODY.

106
00:05:27,762 --> 00:05:30,330
SHE'S 12 YEARS OLD.
DON'T--DON'T YOU GET IT?

107
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,941
IT'S NOT HOMEWORK. IT'S
A PROJECT ABOUT THE PYRAMIDS.

108
00:05:32,941 --> 00:05:35,900
I CAN TALK TO YOU.THANKS, LANIE.

109
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:37,728
SIT RIGHT HERE, SWEETIE.

110
00:05:39,556 --> 00:05:43,168
I'M AGENT LISBON,
AND THAT'S PATRICK JANE.

111
00:05:43,168 --> 00:05:46,824
HI. WHAT DO YOU HAVE TO DO
FOR THE PYRAMID PROJECT?

112
00:05:46,824 --> 00:05:48,391
DESCRIBE THE AFTERLIFE

113
00:05:48,391 --> 00:05:50,915
AS DEPICTED IN
THE ANCIENT EGYPTIAN MYTHOLOGY.

114
00:05:50,915 --> 00:05:54,441
AH, AS DEPICTED IN
THE ANCIENT EGYPTIAN MYTHOLOGY.

115
00:05:54,441 --> 00:05:58,706
WELL, DID YOU KNOW THAT
THEY BELIEVED THAT WHEN YOU DIE,

116
00:05:58,706 --> 00:06:01,535
YOU ARE CARRIED
INTO THE NEXT LIFE

117
00:06:01,535 --> 00:06:04,451
ON THE BACK
OF A SACRED HIPPOPOTAMUS?

118
00:06:04,451 --> 00:06:06,540
THAT'S TRUE.

119
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:09,325
WHAT TIME DID YOU GET HOME
FROM SCHOOL?

120
00:06:09,325 --> 00:06:12,241
A LITTLE AFTER 3:00.WHAT DID YOU DO?

121
00:06:12,241 --> 00:06:15,026
I MADE LEMONADE.
JAMES LOVES MY LEMONADE.

122
00:06:15,026 --> 00:06:16,680
WHO ELSE WAS HOME?

123
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,943
UH, NOBODY. UH,
I WAS AT THE GALLERY,

124
00:06:18,943 --> 00:06:22,120
AND JOLENE WAS AT THE GYM.[Lisbon]
MR. BANKS, PLEASE.

125
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,600
[Lanie] NO ONE WAS HERE.

126
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:26,168
I TOOK THE LEMONADE
TO THE POOL HOUSE.

127
00:06:26,168 --> 00:06:29,650
I-I SAW...

128
00:06:29,650 --> 00:06:34,089
[voice breaking]
SO MUCH BLOOD.

129
00:06:34,089 --> 00:06:36,439
DID YOU SEE ANYBODY
OR HEAR ANYTHING?

130
00:06:36,439 --> 00:06:38,223
VOICES? A CAR?

131
00:06:38,223 --> 00:06:41,444
[crying] JUST JAMES.I'M TAKING HER
UPSTAIRS NOW.

132
00:06:41,444 --> 00:06:44,142
DOES ANYBODY KNOW
WHAT WAS INSIDE THIS?

133
00:06:44,142 --> 00:06:46,406
NO. ARE WE THROUGH?ALMOST.

134
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:49,583
LANIE, WHY DIDN'T YOUR MOTHER
WANT YOU TO SPEAK TO US?

135
00:06:49,583 --> 00:06:51,628
SHE'S NOT MY MOTHER.

136
00:06:51,628 --> 00:06:53,369
HONEY, IT--IT'S OKAY.

137
00:06:53,369 --> 00:06:55,023
I WAS PROTECTING HER.

138
00:06:55,023 --> 00:06:58,069
SHE'S BEEN THROUGH
A VERY TRAUMATIC EXPERIENCE.

139
00:06:58,069 --> 00:07:01,246
OH, I THOUGHT YOU WERE WORRIED
SHE WAS GONNA SAY SOMETHING

140
00:07:01,246 --> 00:07:04,206
ABOUT WHATEVER IT IS YOU'RE
TRYING TO HIDE FROM US.

141
00:07:04,206 --> 00:07:06,164
HOW DARE YOU?

142
00:07:06,164 --> 00:07:07,775
REALLY? HOW DAREI?

143
00:07:07,775 --> 00:07:10,168
IS THAT THE BEST COMEBACK
YOU'VE GOT?

144
00:07:10,168 --> 00:07:15,130
YOU'RE GONNA LET THIS MAN
INSULT ME?HUH?

145
00:07:15,130 --> 00:07:17,959
STAND THERE WITH
YOUR MOUTH OPEN LIKE A MORON.

146
00:07:17,959 --> 00:07:19,961
BABY.[glass clanks]

147
00:07:19,961 --> 00:07:22,267
BABY. REALLY?

148
00:07:22,267 --> 00:07:24,313
WHEW. WELL PLAYED.

149
00:07:24,313 --> 00:07:27,142
YEAH. I'M STARVING.

150
00:07:27,142 --> 00:07:29,536
WE'VE GOT FOUR CAMERAS
IN THE BACKYARD.

151
00:07:29,536 --> 00:07:32,495
WE RAN THE FOOTAGE
FROM SUNUP TILL WE GOT HERE.CHECK THIS OUT.

152
00:07:32,495 --> 00:07:35,498
[tapping keys]WE FOUND THIS AT 2:37.
WATCH THE WINDOW.

153
00:07:35,498 --> 00:07:39,067
IT'S A MUZZLE FLASH.WHO'S IN THERE?
WH-WHAT CAMERA HAD THE DOOR?

154
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:41,504
THIS IS THE ONLY IMAGE
WE'VE GOT.

155
00:07:41,504 --> 00:07:43,114
NOBODY COMING IN OR OUT
OR IN THE YARD?

156
00:07:43,114 --> 00:07:45,073
[mouth full]
WHOEVER SHOT SMITHSON KNEW

157
00:07:45,073 --> 00:07:48,946
WHERE THOSE CAMERAS WERE PLACED
AND HOW TO AVOID 'EM.

158
00:07:48,946 --> 00:07:52,689
THIS ONE'S MINE. IF YOU WANT
ONE, I CAN MAKE ONE FOR YOU.

159
00:07:52,689 --> 00:07:55,039
WE NEED TO CHECK
JOLENE AND HOPPER'S ALIBIS.

160
00:07:55,039 --> 00:07:57,041
YOU KNOW,
HOLD ON A SECOND.

161
00:07:57,041 --> 00:07:59,130
NONE OF THESE CAMERAS ARE
HIDDEN.

162
00:07:59,130 --> 00:08:01,132
ANYONE CAN SEE 'EM--
GUESTS,

163
00:08:01,132 --> 00:08:04,614
STUDENTS COMING HERE
FOR TUTORING, THEIR PARENTS,

164
00:08:04,614 --> 00:08:07,051
EVERYBODY.OH. GOOD POINT.

165
00:08:07,051 --> 00:08:09,053
THANKS FOR YOUR TIME,
MR. BANDINO.

166
00:08:09,053 --> 00:08:11,012
THANK YOU.

167
00:08:11,012 --> 00:08:13,014
CHEERS.

168
00:08:13,014 --> 00:08:14,972
[Van Pelt] THE VICTIM,
JAMES SMITHSON, DOESN'T EXIST.

169
00:08:14,972 --> 00:08:16,974
PASSPORT'S FAKE.
HIS REFERENCES ARE BOGUS.

170
00:08:16,974 --> 00:08:19,629
I RAN HIS PRINTS
THROUGH ALL THE DATABASES.

171
00:08:19,629 --> 00:08:21,588
THERE'S NOTHING,
NOTHING AT ALL.

172
00:08:21,588 --> 00:08:24,547
YOUR FRIEND BANDINO DIDN'T DO
MUCH OF A BACKGROUND CHECK.

173
00:08:24,547 --> 00:08:26,506
MM. THAT'S NOT LIKE HIM.

174
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,986
HE'S NOT THE SHARPEST KNIFE
IN THE DRAWER,

175
00:08:28,986 --> 00:08:31,946
BUT HE ALWAYS DID
THE LEGWORK.DO YOU THINK MAYBE HE'S
HOLDING SOMETHING BACK,

176
00:08:31,946 --> 00:08:34,601
PROTECTING HIS CLIENTS?YEAH, I'LL CHECK IT OUT.

177
00:08:34,601 --> 00:08:36,385
TAKE VAN PELT.

178
00:08:36,385 --> 00:08:38,822
[sighs]

179
00:08:38,822 --> 00:08:41,085
JUST STOP WORRYING.

180
00:08:41,085 --> 00:08:43,566
IT'S GONNA BE FINE
WITH THE NEW BOSS.

181
00:08:43,566 --> 00:08:46,003
I MEAN, SURE, THERE'LL BE
A SETTLING-IN PERIOD

182
00:08:46,003 --> 00:08:49,137
WHEN SHE PROBES YOUR PSYCHE
FOR WEAKNESS,

183
00:08:49,137 --> 00:08:52,227
BUT ONCE THAT'S
OUT OF THE WAY--WOULD YOU STOP?
YOU'RE BEING SO CHILDISH.

184
00:08:52,227 --> 00:08:55,186
I THINK YOU'RE
THE ONE WHO'S NERVOUS.

185
00:08:55,186 --> 00:08:57,145
OOH. THAT SOUNDS PERCEPTIVE.
LET ME THINK ABOUT THAT.

186
00:08:57,145 --> 00:09:00,888
NO. I FIND THAT I'M NOT.
IT'S DEFINITELY YOU.

187
00:09:00,888 --> 00:09:03,325
I'M GONNA GO TALK
TO SMITHSON'S REGULAR STUDENTS

188
00:09:03,325 --> 00:09:06,371
AND THEIR PARENTS,
FILL IN SOME OF THESE BLANKS.GOOD IDEA.
TAKE HIM WITH YOU.

189
00:09:06,371 --> 00:09:08,112
[Cho] COME ON.

190
00:09:08,112 --> 00:09:10,985
[woman] MY GOD.
IT'S SO TERRIBLE.

191
00:09:10,985 --> 00:09:13,030
DO YOU HAVE ANY IDEA
WHO DID IT?

192
00:09:13,030 --> 00:09:15,903
WE'RE STILL INVESTIGATING,
MRS. BLANKMAN.

193
00:09:15,903 --> 00:09:18,079
NOW THE PARENTS AND STUDENTS
WE'VE TALKED TO ALL SAY

194
00:09:18,079 --> 00:09:20,734
HE WAS A GREAT TUTOR,
BUT NOT MUCH ELSE.

195
00:09:20,734 --> 00:09:23,084
HOW WELL DID YOU KNOW
MR. SMITHSON?

196
00:09:23,084 --> 00:09:24,738
NOT THAT WELL.

197
00:09:24,738 --> 00:09:27,436
JAMES HAD ONLY BEEN TUTORING
MY SON FOR...

198
00:09:27,436 --> 00:09:30,700
THREE... FOUR MONTHS.

199
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:33,007
I'D DROP OFF, PICK UP.

200
00:09:33,007 --> 00:09:35,009
YOU KNOW, SAY HELLO.

201
00:09:35,009 --> 00:09:37,011
HE SEEMED NICE.

202
00:09:37,011 --> 00:09:38,447
E-EXCUSE ME,
MRS. BLANKMAN.

203
00:09:38,447 --> 00:09:40,275
I-I'M SORRY.
DON'T MEAN TO INTERRUPT.

204
00:09:40,275 --> 00:09:41,624
I'M A LITTLE PARCHED.

205
00:09:41,624 --> 00:09:44,148
COULD I BOTHER YOU
FOR A CUP OF TEA?

206
00:09:44,148 --> 00:09:47,064
OH. I'M SORRY.
I DIDN'T OFFER YOU--OH, N-N-NO, PLEASE.
I-I CAN GET IT.

207
00:09:47,064 --> 00:09:49,501
YOU'RE SHAKING.
WOULD YOU LIKE A CUP?

208
00:09:49,501 --> 00:09:50,720
UH...CHO?

209
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,939
NO, THANKS.

210
00:10:03,254 --> 00:10:06,040
[sniffs]

211
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:08,085
[sniffs]

212
00:10:08,085 --> 00:10:11,698
[kettle whistling]

213
00:10:11,698 --> 00:10:13,917
[closes cabinet doors]

214
00:10:22,883 --> 00:10:25,755
[spritzing]

215
00:10:34,024 --> 00:10:36,636
YOUR SON NEVER MENTIONED
ANYTHING?

216
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:37,985
MONEY PROBLEMS?
ANYTHING UNUSUAL?

217
00:10:37,985 --> 00:10:39,943
THEY JUST STUDIED.

218
00:10:39,943 --> 00:10:42,511
SMELLED SO GOOD,
I WENT AND MADE YOU ONE.

219
00:10:42,511 --> 00:10:45,035
LEMONGRASS, MY FAVORITE.

220
00:10:45,035 --> 00:10:46,689
[sighs]

221
00:10:46,689 --> 00:10:48,691
YEAH, IT'S FUNNY
HOW SMELLS WORK.

222
00:10:48,691 --> 00:10:52,129
THEY ATTACH THEMSELVES
TO SUCH SPECIFIC MEMORIES.

223
00:10:52,129 --> 00:10:55,089
YOU KNOW, LIKE THE, UH,
KITCHEN OF A CHILDHOOD HOME,

224
00:10:55,089 --> 00:10:57,221
OR HAVING A CUP OF TEA
WITH A LOVER.

225
00:10:57,221 --> 00:10:58,396
[inhales and exhales deeply]

226
00:10:58,396 --> 00:11:01,573
[whispers] YES.

227
00:11:01,573 --> 00:11:04,011
YES.

228
00:11:04,011 --> 00:11:06,013
YES,
YOU AND JAMES WERE LOVERS.

229
00:11:06,013 --> 00:11:09,494
[voice breaking] YES.

230
00:11:09,494 --> 00:11:11,148
MM-HMM.

231
00:11:11,148 --> 00:11:14,151
OH, YOU MIGHT NOT WANT
TO DRINK THAT.

232
00:11:14,151 --> 00:11:16,937
THAT'S
A LITTLE... FUNKY MONKEY.[gasps]

233
00:11:16,937 --> 00:11:19,156
WHAT KIND OF BACKGROUND CHECK
DID YOU DO, VIC?

234
00:11:19,156 --> 00:11:22,203
[Vic] THE USUAL.

235
00:11:22,203 --> 00:11:25,162
I CALLED HIS LAST EMPLOYER.
I CHECKED HIS CREDIT.WELL, JAMES SMITHSON ISN'T
JAMES SMITHSON.

236
00:11:25,162 --> 00:11:28,165
NONE OF IT'S TRUE.WELL, THERE'S A LIMIT
TO WHAT I CAN DO, YOU KNOW?

237
00:11:28,165 --> 00:11:31,125
I'M NOT THE CIA, HERE.AW, COME ON, MAN. YOU USED
TO BE MORE GUNG-HO THAN THAT.

238
00:11:31,125 --> 00:11:33,518
[laughs] THAT'S
WHY I'M NOT A COP ANYMORE.

239
00:11:33,518 --> 00:11:35,477
IT'S TOO STRESSFUL.
UNHEALTHY PROFESSION.

240
00:11:35,477 --> 00:11:37,131
YEAH, NO KIDDING.

241
00:11:37,131 --> 00:11:39,786
HEY, YOU GOT ANYTHING?

242
00:11:39,786 --> 00:11:41,788
SERIOUSLY, YOU HEAR
ABOUT HANK HARRISON?

243
00:11:41,788 --> 00:11:44,312
39 YEARS OLD,
5 YEARS OUT FROM HIS PENSION--

244
00:11:44,312 --> 00:11:47,184
BOOM. HEART ATTACK.
A WIFE, TWO KIDS.

245
00:11:47,184 --> 00:11:49,273
HE HAD THAT, UH,
THAT BACHELOR PARTY, REMEMBER?

246
00:11:49,273 --> 00:11:50,797
UH, NO.

247
00:11:50,797 --> 00:11:52,842
AW, COME ON.
SURE YOU DO.

248
00:11:52,842 --> 00:11:55,889
THE STRIPPER WAS ALL OVER
HIS CASE, I'M TELLING YA.

249
00:11:55,889 --> 00:11:57,978
I BET SHE WAS.

250
00:11:57,978 --> 00:12:01,503
OH. [laughs] OH, HEY.
ARE YOU TWO, LIKE, UH--

251
00:12:01,503 --> 00:12:03,505
ARE YOU DATING EACH OTHER?

252
00:12:03,505 --> 00:12:05,420
NO, WE'RE NOT.NO.

253
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:08,162
NO? BECAUSE YOU BOTH LOOKED
A LITTLE WEIRD JUST NOW.NO.

254
00:12:08,162 --> 00:12:10,294
WE'RE TALKING
ABOUT A MURDER HERE.

255
00:12:10,294 --> 00:12:13,297
YEAH. YEAH, HEY, LOOK,
I'M SORRY, ALL RIGHT?

256
00:12:13,297 --> 00:12:15,343
UH, THERE IS ONE THING.

257
00:12:15,343 --> 00:12:18,912
A COUPLE MONTHS AGO, HOPPER WAS
WORKING ON THIS PHOTO THING.

258
00:12:18,912 --> 00:12:21,653
HE, UH--HE ASKED ME
TO GET HIM A GUN.

259
00:12:21,653 --> 00:12:24,004
OLD-FASHIONED PIECE,
LIKE THE FBI WAS USING

260
00:12:24,004 --> 00:12:26,441
IN SOME '60s MOVIE HE SAW.LIKE A .38?

261
00:12:26,441 --> 00:12:28,660
YEAH, I GUESS.

262
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:30,706
WE NEVER GOT TO THAT.
I TURNED HIM DOWN.

263
00:12:30,706 --> 00:12:33,491
TOLD HIM IF HE WANTED IT
LIKE THE MOVIE, GET A PROP GUN.

264
00:12:33,491 --> 00:12:36,233
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT HE DID IN THE END,

265
00:12:36,233 --> 00:12:39,497
BUT IT'S WORTH MENTIONING,
RIGHT?YEAH. YEAH, IT IS.
THANKS, MAN. APPRECIATE IT.

266
00:12:39,497 --> 00:12:41,412
HEY, ABSOLUTELY.THANKS FOR YOUR HELP.

267
00:12:41,412 --> 00:12:43,545
YEAH, NO PROBLEM.
HEY, LISTEN.

268
00:12:43,545 --> 00:12:46,504
WHAT SAY YOU AND ME GO GET A CUP
OF COFFEE SOME TIME? [chuckles]NO, THANKS.

269
00:12:46,504 --> 00:12:49,116
HUH? WHAT'S COFFEE?
I'M A NICE GUY, RIGHT, RIGS?

270
00:12:49,116 --> 00:12:51,074
SEE YA LATER, VIC.

271
00:12:51,074 --> 00:12:54,512
[Cho] SO SMITHSON WAS
A BIG LADIES' MAN,

272
00:12:54,512 --> 00:12:56,601
AND THEY'VE BOTH GOT
SOLID ALIBIS.

273
00:12:56,601 --> 00:12:59,387
MAGGIE BLANKMAN'S HUSBAND'S BEEN
IN RENO FOR THE LAST THREE DAYS,

274
00:12:59,387 --> 00:13:02,042
AND MAGGIE WAS
AT A THERAPIST'S SESSION

275
00:13:02,042 --> 00:13:04,958
FROM 2:00 TO 4:00 P.M.--
DOUBLE SESSION.JANE AND I ARE GONNA GO
TO HOPPER'S GALLERY,

276
00:13:04,958 --> 00:13:06,568
ASK ABOUT THE GUN.

277
00:13:06,568 --> 00:13:09,571
[exhales deeply]

278
00:13:09,571 --> 00:13:11,138
HEY. [sighs]

279
00:13:11,138 --> 00:13:14,141
[tapping keys]

280
00:13:14,141 --> 00:13:16,491
WANT A COFFEE?

281
00:13:16,491 --> 00:13:19,929
NO, THANKS.
SO WHAT WAS HER NAME?

282
00:13:19,929 --> 00:13:21,061
WHO?

283
00:13:21,061 --> 00:13:22,889
THE STRIPPER.

284
00:13:22,889 --> 00:13:25,282
O-OH. I, UH...

285
00:13:25,282 --> 00:13:26,893
WE COULD DOUBLE-DATE--

286
00:13:26,893 --> 00:13:28,285
ME AND BANDINO,

287
00:13:28,285 --> 00:13:30,026
YOU AND YOUR STRIPPER.

288
00:13:30,026 --> 00:13:32,942
WH--I TH--
I THOUGHT Y-YOU...

289
00:13:32,942 --> 00:13:35,075
[laughs]

290
00:13:35,075 --> 00:13:36,424
OH. [laughs]

291
00:13:36,424 --> 00:13:38,165
THAT'S MEAN.

292
00:13:38,165 --> 00:13:40,123
KIDDING.

293
00:13:40,123 --> 00:13:42,125
OH, HER NAME WAS,
UH, KANDY.

294
00:13:42,125 --> 00:13:44,171
OH, YEAH.
SWEET KANDY, WITH A "K."

295
00:13:44,171 --> 00:13:46,216
[singsongy] OH.

296
00:13:46,216 --> 00:13:49,263
[normal voice]
KANDY WITH A "K." MM-HMM.[typing]

297
00:13:51,395 --> 00:13:53,397
DO I OWN A GUN?

298
00:13:53,397 --> 00:13:55,443
YES, MR. BANKS, A .38.[sighs]

299
00:13:55,443 --> 00:13:58,446
HAVE YOU EVER BEEN IN
POSSESSION OF ONE OR OWNED ONE?

300
00:13:58,446 --> 00:14:01,057
I NEVER HAD A GUN,
ANY KIND.

301
00:14:01,057 --> 00:14:03,016
I DON'T BELIEVE IN THEM.

302
00:14:03,016 --> 00:14:05,061
YOU'RE JUST NOT TRYING
HARD ENOUGH.

303
00:14:05,061 --> 00:14:07,455
I AM. YOU JUST
CAN'T READ MINDS.

304
00:14:07,455 --> 00:14:09,936
YOU CLOSE YOUR EYES, OKAY?
I'M THE BOSS HERE.

305
00:14:09,936 --> 00:14:12,677
CONCENTRATE.

306
00:14:12,677 --> 00:14:15,855
IT'S COMING TO ME.
CHOCOLATE...

307
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:18,509
COCONUT...

308
00:14:18,509 --> 00:14:20,990
SWIRL. HUH?

309
00:14:20,990 --> 00:14:22,600
VANILLA.

310
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,993
PAY UP.

311
00:14:23,993 --> 00:14:25,995
THAT'S NOT FUNNY.

312
00:14:25,995 --> 00:14:29,999
[laughs] YEAH, IT IS. HEY,
DAD, JUST GETTING ICE CREAM.

313
00:14:29,999 --> 00:14:31,914
OKAY.

314
00:14:31,914 --> 00:14:34,395
UH, WOULD YOU MIND
TAKING A POLYGRAPH TEST?

315
00:14:34,395 --> 00:14:36,005
NO. WHY WOULD I DO THAT?

316
00:14:36,005 --> 00:14:38,355
I'LL GIVE YOU THIS,
HOPPER--

317
00:14:38,355 --> 00:14:40,357
YOU HAVE
A VERY CONSISTENT VISION.

318
00:14:40,357 --> 00:14:43,360
A LITTLE CRAZY,
BUT CONSISTENT.

319
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:46,581
[Hopper] I WOULDN'T EXPECT YOU
TO UNDERSTAND WHAT I'M DOING.

320
00:14:46,581 --> 00:14:49,018
LET ME GIVE IT A SHOT.

321
00:14:49,018 --> 00:14:51,629
YOU ENJOY TAKING POSSESSION
OF YOUR WIFE,

322
00:14:51,629 --> 00:14:54,023
BUT ONLY ON CAMERA,
NOT IN THE FLESH.

323
00:14:54,023 --> 00:14:56,808
YOU WERE BEING CUCKOLDED
BY JAMES SMITHSON,

324
00:14:56,808 --> 00:14:58,854
AND YOU LET IT HAPPEN.

325
00:14:58,854 --> 00:15:01,291
WHY?
IMPOTENCE? MASOCHISM?

326
00:15:01,291 --> 00:15:03,250
HOMOSEXUALITY?

327
00:15:03,250 --> 00:15:05,600
I'M NOT SURE.

328
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:08,995
[laughs] THAT'S VERY PERCEPTIVE,
MR. JANE. YOU HAVE A TALENT.

329
00:15:08,995 --> 00:15:11,258
MEH, IT'S JUST...
I DO. THANKS.

330
00:15:11,258 --> 00:15:13,260
IT'S JUST...
IT'S AN EASY CALL.

331
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:16,045
YOU'RE VERY ATTRACTIVE
BUT UNHAPPY

332
00:15:16,045 --> 00:15:19,788
AND ACCUSTOMED TO USING
YOUR SEXUALITY AS A WEAPON.

333
00:15:19,788 --> 00:15:23,270
DID YOU USE YOUR SEXUALITY
AS A WEAPON AGAINST HIM?

334
00:15:23,270 --> 00:15:26,838
OKAY, YOU'RE DONE.
NOW... GO.

335
00:15:26,838 --> 00:15:29,450
WHAT DOES IT TAKE
TO GET YOU MAD, HOPPER?

336
00:15:29,450 --> 00:15:32,322
DID SMITHSON RUB YOUR NOSE
IN IT?THAT'S RIDICULOUS!

337
00:15:32,322 --> 00:15:34,585
WHAT'S WRONG?

338
00:15:34,585 --> 00:15:38,285
UH, NOTHING, HONEY. UH,
THESE PEOPLE WERE JUST LEAVING.YEAH, WE SHOULD LEAVE.

339
00:15:38,285 --> 00:15:40,113
LET'S. YEAH.

340
00:15:40,113 --> 00:15:42,071
OKAY.
HOW'S THE ICE CREAM?GOOD.

341
00:15:42,071 --> 00:15:44,030
YEAH.
HARD TO BEAT VANILLA.

342
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:50,688
[Lisbon] I KNOW, I KNOW.

343
00:15:50,688 --> 00:15:53,691
YOU WERE MAKING STUFF UP
TO GET THE GUY ANGRY

344
00:15:53,691 --> 00:15:57,347
SO YOU COULD GET A READ
ON HIM. BLAH, BLAH, BLAH.

345
00:15:57,347 --> 00:15:59,567
THE TRUTH IS,
YOU JUST DIDN'T LIKE THE GUY.

346
00:15:59,567 --> 00:16:03,136
WELL, THAT WOULD BE
VERY UNPROFESSIONAL.

347
00:16:03,136 --> 00:16:06,356
UM, COULD YOU TAKE
THE NEXT LEFT, PLEASE?

348
00:16:06,356 --> 00:16:09,142
OKAY.
WELL, WHAT DID YOU READ?

349
00:16:09,142 --> 00:16:11,144
DID HE DO IT?

350
00:16:11,144 --> 00:16:13,146
TAKE THE NEXT LEFT,
AND I'LL TELL YOU.

351
00:16:16,888 --> 00:16:19,108
WELL?

352
00:16:19,108 --> 00:16:21,502
WELL, MAYBE.
HE HAD A GOOD MOTIVE.

353
00:16:21,502 --> 00:16:24,026
AND MAYBE NOT.
THE RED BOX DIDN'T FIT.

354
00:16:24,026 --> 00:16:26,289
YOU PICKED UP A TAIL?

355
00:16:28,509 --> 00:16:30,076
CUL-DE-SAC.

356
00:16:38,171 --> 00:16:41,043
[turns off engine]

357
00:16:45,178 --> 00:16:47,180
[sighs]

358
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:49,312
NOTHING.

359
00:16:49,312 --> 00:16:53,142
YOU SURE?

360
00:16:53,142 --> 00:16:54,796
UH-HUH.

361
00:17:05,111 --> 00:17:07,113
EXCUSE ME.

362
00:17:07,113 --> 00:17:09,724
WHY ARE YOU FOLLOWING US?

363
00:17:09,724 --> 00:17:11,726
[Southern accent]
FOLLOWING YOU?

364
00:17:11,726 --> 00:17:15,164
SHOOT, I THOUGHT
CALIFORNIA WAS FRIENDLY.

365
00:17:15,164 --> 00:17:18,037
I'M JUST TRYING TO MAKE
A SALE HERE--LIFE INSURANCE.

366
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:20,517
CUTE YOUNG COUPLE
LIKE YOURSELVES,

367
00:17:20,517 --> 00:17:22,867
NOW YOU'VE GOTTA THINK
ABOUT THE FUTURE, RIGHT?

368
00:17:22,867 --> 00:17:24,826
YOU GOT KIDS YET?

369
00:17:24,826 --> 00:17:27,176
THAT'S A TERRIBLE ACCENT.
DISGUISED BRITISH, YES?

370
00:17:27,176 --> 00:17:29,831
YOU GOTTA WORK ON
YOUR GLOTTAL STOP.

371
00:17:29,831 --> 00:17:33,008
HIS WHAT?[mouth full]
HIS GLOTTAL STOP.

372
00:17:33,008 --> 00:17:35,228
CAN WE SEE
SOME IDENTIFICATION, PLEASE?

373
00:17:35,228 --> 00:17:38,883
UH, SURE. IT'S IN THE CAR.
I'LL--HOLD ON, I'LL GET IT.UH-OH.

374
00:17:38,883 --> 00:17:41,277
PUT YOUR HANDS ON THE CAR.
NOW.

375
00:17:43,497 --> 00:17:45,760
WHAT'S THIS ABOUT?

376
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:47,196
TURN AROUND.

377
00:17:47,196 --> 00:17:50,417
A STRANGER ASKS TO SEE
YOUR I.D.,

378
00:17:50,417 --> 00:17:52,897
YOU ASK THEM
TO SHOW YOU THEIRS FIRST.

379
00:17:52,897 --> 00:17:57,163
UNLESS, OF COURSE, YOU'RE
TRYING TO HIDE SOMETHING.

380
00:17:57,163 --> 00:17:59,904
[British accent] QUITE RIGHT.
QUITE RIGHT, MR. JANE.

381
00:17:59,904 --> 00:18:01,384
[chuckles]

382
00:18:01,384 --> 00:18:03,734
WHO ARE YOU?

383
00:18:03,734 --> 00:18:05,736
[sighs] FRANCIS SLOCOMBE.
INSPECTOR FRANCIS SLOCOMBE.

384
00:18:05,736 --> 00:18:07,521
SCOTLAND YARD
SPECIAL BRANCH.

385
00:18:07,521 --> 00:18:09,523
EH.

386
00:18:09,523 --> 00:18:11,873
[crunches]

387
00:18:12,830 --> 00:18:14,441
[Cho] THANK YOU.

388
00:18:14,441 --> 00:18:15,877
[hangs up telephone receiver]

389
00:18:15,877 --> 00:18:18,488
I CAN'T REACH YOUR CONTACT
AT SCOTLAND YARD.

390
00:18:18,488 --> 00:18:20,447
TIME DIFFERENCE.
TRICKY ONE, THAT.

391
00:18:20,447 --> 00:18:21,709
YEP, FRANCIS SLOCOMBE,

392
00:18:21,709 --> 00:18:23,102
REGISTERED
AT THE FLAMINGO HOTEL.

393
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:25,930
WHERE'S JANE?HERE.

394
00:18:25,930 --> 00:18:28,846
OH, THANKS. LOVELY.
DID YOU CHECK LIVERPOOL'S SCORE?UP 1-NOTHING.
END OF THE FIRST HALF.

395
00:18:28,846 --> 00:18:30,109
EXCELLENT.

396
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:31,762
WHERE ARE
THE CUCUMBER SANDWICHES?

397
00:18:31,762 --> 00:18:34,374
I'M BEING NICE TO HIM,

398
00:18:34,374 --> 00:18:37,507
BECAUSE I THINK HE MIGHT KNOW
WHAT WAS IN THIS.OH, WHAT ABOUT
OUR SEARCH WARRANT

399
00:18:37,507 --> 00:18:40,119
THAT GOT KILLED?
FOR THE MURDER WEAPON?YOU'RE NOT EVEN
A BIT CURIOUS?

400
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:42,121
AFTER YOUR PERFORMANCE
AT THE GALLERY,

401
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:44,688
BANKS MADE
SOME PHONE CALLS.

402
00:18:44,688 --> 00:18:47,082
NOW JUDGE WITHERS WON'T SIGN
THE WARRANT.OOPS. SORRY.
UH, SHE'S A LITTLE CRANKY.

403
00:18:47,082 --> 00:18:50,129
NEW BOSS COMING IN.ENOUGH WITH THAT.
DID HIS STORY CHECK OUT?

404
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:53,349
NOPE.ABOUT JAMES SMITHSON--
HIS REAL NAME'S OLIVER STANS.

405
00:18:53,349 --> 00:18:55,699
NINE MONTHS AGO HE STOLE
AN EXTREMELY VALUABLE ARTIFACT

406
00:18:55,699 --> 00:18:57,397
FROM THE BRITISH MUSEUM--

407
00:18:57,397 --> 00:19:00,704
A PRISTINE EXAMPLE OF
GRECO-ROMAN ART CIRCA 50 B.C.

408
00:19:00,704 --> 00:19:03,664
A WEDDING RING,
SAID TO BELONG TO CLEOPATRA,

409
00:19:03,664 --> 00:19:06,362
GIVEN HER BY MARK ANTONY.

410
00:19:06,362 --> 00:19:08,364
THAT'S WHAT WAS IN THE BOX.

411
00:19:08,364 --> 00:19:09,931
AH.

412
00:19:09,931 --> 00:19:11,672
HERE'S A COPY

413
00:19:11,672 --> 00:19:14,892
FROM THE MUSEUM GIFT SHOP.

414
00:19:14,892 --> 00:19:17,286
STANS LIFTED THE RING

415
00:19:17,286 --> 00:19:19,680
AND REPLACED IT
WITH ONE OF THOSE.

416
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:22,900
WHAT WAS HE DOING
IN THE UNITED STATES?

417
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:25,164
HE KNEW WE WERE BUILDING
A CASE AGAINST HIM.

418
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,253
CHANGED HIS NAME,
DISAPPEARED.

419
00:19:27,253 --> 00:19:29,864
A WEEK AGO
WE PICKED UP CHATTER

420
00:19:29,864 --> 00:19:31,779
THAT A DEALER
IN STOLEN ANTIQUITIES

421
00:19:31,779 --> 00:19:34,999
WAS GONNA BUY THE RING HERE,
HAD SENT SOMEONE TO PICK IT UP.

422
00:19:34,999 --> 00:19:37,176
MAY I?

423
00:19:41,005 --> 00:19:42,790
THIS IS LOUIS ANGLET...

424
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:46,272
[clicks]GO-TO COURIER IN
THE HIGH-END STOLEN ART MARKET.

425
00:19:46,272 --> 00:19:48,230
I FOLLOWED HIM HERE
TO STANS AND THE RING,

426
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:49,927
BUT I ARRIVED TOO LATE.

427
00:19:49,927 --> 00:19:51,668
THAT'S WHY
I WAS FOLLOWING YOU.

428
00:19:51,668 --> 00:19:53,931
[sighs]
ANGLET HAS THE RING NOW,

429
00:19:53,931 --> 00:19:56,151
AND I NEED TO GET BACK
ON THE TRAIL.

430
00:19:56,151 --> 00:19:58,762
YOU'RE NOT GOING ANYWHERE
UNTIL YOUR STORY CHECKS OUT.

431
00:19:58,762 --> 00:20:01,287
WHOEVER KILLED STANS
KILLED HIM FOR THE RING.

432
00:20:01,287 --> 00:20:04,115
RON, TAKE MR. SLOCOMBE
TO AN INTERROGATION ROOM.

433
00:20:04,115 --> 00:20:07,510
SIT ON HIM
WHILE I MAKE A CALL.

434
00:20:07,510 --> 00:20:08,859
SURE.

435
00:20:08,859 --> 00:20:10,470
[handcuffs click]

436
00:20:10,470 --> 00:20:12,341
LET'S GO.

437
00:20:14,822 --> 00:20:18,652
SLOCOMBE'S RIGHT.
JAMES SMITHSON IS OLIVER STANS.

438
00:20:18,652 --> 00:20:21,829
A FEW MINOR ARRESTS--
NARCOTICS POSSESSION CHARGE,

439
00:20:21,829 --> 00:20:23,309
ASSAULT.
LOOKS LIKE A BAR FIGHT.

440
00:20:23,309 --> 00:20:26,094
[typing]

441
00:20:26,094 --> 00:20:29,706
AND YES, A PERSON OF INTEREST
IN THE BRITISH MUSEUM THEFT.ANY NEXT OF KIN?
THE HOSPITAL CALLED.

442
00:20:29,706 --> 00:20:32,187
THEY NEED SOMEONE TO SIGN OFF
ON ORGAN DONATION.

443
00:20:32,187 --> 00:20:34,755
UH... STANS' MOTHER WAS
A SINGLE PARENT.

444
00:20:34,755 --> 00:20:37,105
DIED THREE YEARS AGO.
NO SIBLINGS.

445
00:20:37,105 --> 00:20:38,585
[Lisbon]
CHO, COME WITH ME.

446
00:20:38,585 --> 00:20:41,065
WE NEED TO ASK SLOCOMBE
SOME QUESTIONS.

447
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:46,070
[gasps] HIS GUN'S GONE.

448
00:20:46,070 --> 00:20:48,377
I'LL GET
A SEARCH STARTED.

449
00:20:48,377 --> 00:20:50,423
RON, CAN YOU HEAR ME?

450
00:20:50,423 --> 00:20:51,641
[groans]

451
00:20:51,641 --> 00:20:53,730
FBI SAYS HE'S SCOTLAND YARD,

452
00:20:53,730 --> 00:20:56,124
BUT HE'S GOT NOTHING TO DO
WITH THIS CASE.

453
00:20:56,124 --> 00:20:58,735
NINE MONTHS AGO
WHEN THE RING WAS LIFTED,

454
00:20:58,735 --> 00:21:00,737
HE WENT OFF THE RESERVATION.

455
00:21:00,737 --> 00:21:03,218
HE'S BEEN TRACKING STANS
EVER SINCE.HMM.

456
00:21:03,218 --> 00:21:05,916
YOU THINK
HE HELPED WITH THE ROBBERY,

457
00:21:05,916 --> 00:21:09,224
AND STANS
DOUBLE-CROSSED HIM?NO. NO, SLOCOMBE'S JUST TRYING
TO GET THE RING BACK.

458
00:21:09,224 --> 00:21:12,488
"WHY?" IS THE BIG QUESTION.

459
00:21:12,488 --> 00:21:15,361
[Lisbon] YOU TWO,
GO TO HIS MOTEL ROOM.

460
00:21:15,361 --> 00:21:18,973
SEE IF YOU CAN FIND ANYTHING
THERE THAT'LL HELP US.OKAY.

461
00:21:18,973 --> 00:21:22,846
HEY, NO SIGN OF SLOCOMBE.
I GOT A GRID SEARCH STARTED.

462
00:21:22,846 --> 00:21:24,892
THIS IS PERFECT.
IT'S PERFECT.

463
00:21:24,892 --> 00:21:27,677
[telephone ringing in distance]

464
00:21:27,677 --> 00:21:29,940
AGENT LISBON.

465
00:21:31,986 --> 00:21:33,640
MADELEINE HIGHTOWER.

466
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:36,382
SPECIAL AGENT HIGHTOWER,
WELCOME.THANK YOU.

467
00:21:36,382 --> 00:21:37,774
THIS IS PATRICK JANE.

468
00:21:37,774 --> 00:21:40,603
THE FAMOUS MR. JANE.

469
00:21:40,603 --> 00:21:42,823
MM-HMM.

470
00:21:42,823 --> 00:21:44,955
GOOD TO MEET YOU.YOU, TOO.

471
00:21:44,955 --> 00:21:47,567
I THOUGHT I'D HAVE
A NICE, QUIET DAY TODAY,

472
00:21:47,567 --> 00:21:49,656
BUT IT SEEMS LIKE
THERE'S TROUBLE.

473
00:21:49,656 --> 00:21:52,746
WE LOST SOMEBODY.

474
00:21:52,746 --> 00:21:54,878
WE'RE LOOKING FOR HIM.

475
00:21:54,878 --> 00:21:57,446
THEN I'M SURE
YOU'LL FIND HIM.

476
00:21:59,230 --> 00:22:01,842
LET'S TALK IN MY OFFICE.

477
00:22:01,842 --> 00:22:04,192
GIVE ME A HALF-HOUR
TO ROLL SOME CALLS.

478
00:22:04,192 --> 00:22:07,021
YES, MA'AM.

479
00:22:10,677 --> 00:22:14,333
SHE LIKES YOU.
I CAN TELL.

480
00:22:19,816 --> 00:22:23,429
[Rigsby] I'VE STAYED
IN WORSE PLACES.

481
00:22:23,429 --> 00:22:26,519
THAT'S SHOCKING.[singsongy] OH.

482
00:22:26,519 --> 00:22:28,521
[bed squeaking][normal voice] OH. OH, WOW.

483
00:22:28,521 --> 00:22:31,872
THAT IS A GOOD BED
FOR A MOTEL ROOM. VERY FIRM.

484
00:22:31,872 --> 00:22:33,656
UH-HUH.

485
00:22:33,656 --> 00:22:35,789
YOU, UH... YOU WANNA TRY IT?

486
00:22:35,789 --> 00:22:37,573
OH, COME ON.

487
00:22:37,573 --> 00:22:40,663
WHAT? THERE'S NOBODY HERE.
WE CAN LOCK THE DOOR.

488
00:22:40,663 --> 00:22:42,056
NOBODY'S LOOKING.[sighs]

489
00:22:42,056 --> 00:22:44,537
COME ON.WE'RE ON DUTY.

490
00:22:44,537 --> 00:22:46,713
YEAH, I KNOW.
TOTALLYWRONG.

491
00:22:48,671 --> 00:22:50,281
[laughs] COME ON.

492
00:22:50,281 --> 00:22:53,197
[laughs][closes drawer]

493
00:22:53,197 --> 00:22:55,852
WHAT?

494
00:22:55,852 --> 00:22:57,724
HOLD THAT THOUGHT.

495
00:23:01,684 --> 00:23:04,078
WHAT YOU GOT?

496
00:23:04,078 --> 00:23:06,123
EUREKA.

497
00:23:06,123 --> 00:23:09,300
YEAH, EUREKA. NOW DOES THAT MEAN
YOU CAN GET BACK HERE?

498
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:11,694
THIS COULD BE
CRITICAL EVIDENCE.YES, IT COULD BE,

499
00:23:11,694 --> 00:23:13,957
BUT UNLESS THE CRITICAL EVIDENCE
SELF-DESTRUCTS

500
00:23:13,957 --> 00:23:16,003
IN LESS THAN TEN SECONDS,

501
00:23:16,003 --> 00:23:18,179
I SUGGEST
YOU GET YOURSELF BACK HERE.[pats bed]

502
00:23:18,179 --> 00:23:20,834
IT'S CRITICAL.

503
00:23:20,834 --> 00:23:22,662
[laughs]

504
00:23:22,662 --> 00:23:25,273
[giggles] FINE.

505
00:23:25,273 --> 00:23:28,015
[bed squeaks]

506
00:23:28,015 --> 00:23:30,017
MM. MM.MM.

507
00:23:30,017 --> 00:23:31,758
[door opens]

508
00:23:31,758 --> 00:23:33,760
OOH.[door creaks]

509
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:35,762
[clears throat]

510
00:23:35,762 --> 00:23:37,328
[clears throat]

511
00:23:37,328 --> 00:23:39,156
ROOM'S GOOD. THANK YOU.YEAH.

512
00:23:41,724 --> 00:23:43,204
[knock on door]

513
00:23:43,204 --> 00:23:45,685
[Hightower] COME IN.

514
00:23:49,340 --> 00:23:50,951
MA'AM, I ASSURE YOU,

515
00:23:50,951 --> 00:23:53,475
TODAY'S INCIDENT IS NOT
AT ALL INDICATIVE

516
00:23:53,475 --> 00:23:56,913
OF THE UNIT'S
OVERALL CONFIDENCE.

517
00:23:56,913 --> 00:24:00,351
YOU HAD A BAD DAY,
AGENT LISBON.

518
00:24:00,351 --> 00:24:01,744
YOU SCREWED UP.

519
00:24:01,744 --> 00:24:03,746
IT HAPPENS.

520
00:24:03,746 --> 00:24:06,314
NOW LET'S GET TO THE WORK.

521
00:24:06,314 --> 00:24:08,534
THIS JUDGE,
THE ONE WHO CHANGED HIS MIND

522
00:24:08,534 --> 00:24:10,666
ABOUT GIVING US
OUR SEARCH WARRANT--

523
00:24:10,666 --> 00:24:12,494
JUDGE WITHERS, MA'AM.

524
00:24:12,494 --> 00:24:14,235
HE'S KINDA LIKE
A STUBBORN OLD BULL--

525
00:24:14,235 --> 00:24:16,542
WON'T BUDGE
ONCE HE TAKES A POSITION.

526
00:24:16,542 --> 00:24:19,980
I'M TRYING TO GET HIM
ON THE PHONE.AND HE CHANGED HIS MIND
BECAUSE?

527
00:24:19,980 --> 00:24:22,591
HE SAID WE HADN'T MET
THE THRESHOLD.

528
00:24:22,591 --> 00:24:24,854
NOT WHAT HE SAID.

529
00:24:24,854 --> 00:24:26,508
THE REAL REASON.

530
00:24:28,249 --> 00:24:29,729
[sighs]

531
00:24:29,729 --> 00:24:31,731
PATRICK JANE INSULTED
HOPPER BANKS,

532
00:24:31,731 --> 00:24:35,474
AND HOPPER BANKS COMPLAINED.JANE HAS UNUSUAL METHODS,
BUT--

533
00:24:35,474 --> 00:24:37,519
HE CLOSES CASES,
YES, HE DOES.

534
00:24:37,519 --> 00:24:40,653
HE'S A VALUABLE ASSET.
WE CANNOT AFFORD TO LOSE HIM.

535
00:24:40,653 --> 00:24:42,829
THE WAY I SEE IT...

536
00:24:42,829 --> 00:24:46,049
[sighs] IT'S YOU
THAT'S IN A TRICKY SPOT.

537
00:24:46,049 --> 00:24:48,487
MA'AM?

538
00:24:48,487 --> 00:24:51,098
THIS BUREAU HAS SEEN
SOME TOUGH TIMES LATELY.

539
00:24:51,098 --> 00:24:54,188
MY MISSION IS TO TURN THAT
AROUND AND MAKE THE CBI

540
00:24:54,188 --> 00:24:58,714
THE PREMIER LAW ENFORCEMENT
AGENCY IN THIS STATE.

541
00:24:58,714 --> 00:25:00,934
PATRICK JANE IS A HUGE PART
OF THAT GOAL.

542
00:25:05,155 --> 00:25:07,506
IF YOU CAN'T KEEP HIM
IN LINE,

543
00:25:07,506 --> 00:25:10,160
WE'LL FIND SOMEONE WHO CAN.

544
00:25:11,858 --> 00:25:14,077
YES, MA'AM.

545
00:25:14,077 --> 00:25:16,384
YOU CAN GO.

546
00:25:16,384 --> 00:25:18,342
I'LL GIVE JUDGE WITHERS
A CALL,

547
00:25:18,342 --> 00:25:20,344
GET YOU A WARRANT.

548
00:25:20,344 --> 00:25:24,000
[dialing]

549
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:27,090
HEY, BOSS. ACCORDING TO
THE INFORMATION SLOCOMBE DUG UP,

550
00:25:27,090 --> 00:25:29,832
LOUIS ANGLET DOESN'T JUST DEAL
IN STOLEN ANTIQUITIES.

551
00:25:29,832 --> 00:25:31,834
HE'S A HIRED GUN,
NEVER INDICTED,

552
00:25:31,834 --> 00:25:33,923
BUT A PRIME SUSPECT
IN THREE KILLS.

553
00:25:33,923 --> 00:25:35,969
AND HE HASN'T LEFT THE COUNTRY.
HE'S STILL HERE.

554
00:25:35,969 --> 00:25:39,407
MULTIPLE I.D.s, MULTIPLE
ARRESTS, BUT NO JAIL TIME.

555
00:25:39,407 --> 00:25:42,323
HE'S A SLIPPERY CUSTOMER.
HE LOOKS GOOD FOR IT.WE DON'T EVEN KNOW
WHERE ANGLET IS.

556
00:25:42,323 --> 00:25:44,064
WHAT WE DO KNOW IS

557
00:25:44,064 --> 00:25:46,283
THAT EVERY TIME SLOCOMBE
OPENS HIS MOUTH, HE LIES.

558
00:25:46,283 --> 00:25:48,285
WE'VE GOT A BOLO OUT ON HIM.
IN THE MEANTIME,

559
00:25:48,285 --> 00:25:50,549
LET'S JUST PURSUE
THE CASE WE'RE DEVELOPING.

560
00:25:50,549 --> 00:25:52,638
HOPPER BANKS IS STILL
OUR PRIME SUSPECT.

561
00:25:52,638 --> 00:25:55,118
LET'S CHECK OUT HIS HOUSE
FOR THE GUN.

562
00:25:55,118 --> 00:25:57,860
WE DON'T HAVE A SEARCH WARRANT.WE DO NOW.

563
00:25:57,860 --> 00:26:00,036
HIGHTOWER GOT WITHERS
TO SIGN OFF ON IT.

564
00:26:00,036 --> 00:26:03,170
HEY.HEY, ABOUT THE GUN--
DID YOU FIND ANYTHING?

565
00:26:03,170 --> 00:26:06,129
IF YOU DID, I HOPE YOU KEEP
MY NAME OUT OF IT--GO AWAY, MR. BANDINO.

566
00:26:06,129 --> 00:26:08,784
NOTHING SO FAR.
I GOT SOME MORE GUYS COMING.

567
00:26:08,784 --> 00:26:11,831
IT'S A BIG HOUSE.AGENT LISBON, WHAT IS
THE CBI EQUIVALENT OF SIBERIA?

568
00:26:11,831 --> 00:26:14,877
BECAUSE WHATEVER IT IS,
THAT'S WHERE YOU'RE GOING.HOLD THAT THOUGHT, MR. BANKS.

569
00:26:14,877 --> 00:26:17,663
LOOK WHAT I FOUND
IN THE HOME OFFICE.

570
00:26:17,663 --> 00:26:20,579
IT'S A PICTURE OF A PROP.IT'S A PICTURE OF A COLT,
DETECTIVE SPECIAL,

571
00:26:20,579 --> 00:26:22,624
.38 CALIBER, 4-INCH BARREL--

572
00:26:22,624 --> 00:26:25,584
THE SAME KIND OF GUN
KILLED OUR VICTIM.A PROP.

573
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:28,717
WHY DON'T WE SORT OUT WHICH ONE
AT OUR OFFICES, MR. BANKS?

574
00:26:28,717 --> 00:26:31,590
[monitor beeping rhythmically]

575
00:26:36,072 --> 00:26:39,249
[lowered voice] OH, OLIVER,
YOU IDIOT.

576
00:26:39,249 --> 00:26:41,556
YOU BLOODY IDIOT.

577
00:26:43,993 --> 00:26:45,212
[chair scrapes floor]

578
00:26:46,866 --> 00:26:48,824
WHO'S THAT?

579
00:26:48,824 --> 00:26:51,566
COME OUT OR I WILL SHOOT.

580
00:26:57,920 --> 00:27:01,054
UH, I CHECKED FOR YOU.

581
00:27:01,054 --> 00:27:03,012
LIVERPOOL LOST.

582
00:27:03,012 --> 00:27:05,841
BAD SEASON, HUH?

583
00:27:05,841 --> 00:27:07,974
INJURIES.

584
00:27:07,974 --> 00:27:11,107
YOU'RE EXPECTING ME, THEN?

585
00:27:11,107 --> 00:27:12,500
NICE WORK.

586
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:14,197
OH, YOU DROPPED EVERYTHING,

587
00:27:14,197 --> 00:27:17,940
YOU RISKED YOUR WHOLE CAREER

588
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:21,814
TO, UH, FIND HIM BEFORE
YOUR COLLEAGUES AT THE YARD.

589
00:27:21,814 --> 00:27:24,251
YOU FOLLOWED US
AFTER HE WAS SHOT.

590
00:27:24,251 --> 00:27:26,470
YOU'RE BOTH LIVERPOOL FANS.

591
00:27:26,470 --> 00:27:29,038
HE'S FAMILY.

592
00:27:29,038 --> 00:27:32,041
YOUR SON?

593
00:27:32,041 --> 00:27:34,261
YEAH.

594
00:27:34,261 --> 00:27:37,612
MY SON.

595
00:27:39,396 --> 00:27:43,183
I WAS NO FATHER TO HIM.

596
00:27:43,183 --> 00:27:45,968
NEVER MARRIED HIS MOTHER.

597
00:27:45,968 --> 00:27:48,405
NEVER SPENT TIME WITH HIM
AT ALL, REALLY.

598
00:27:50,190 --> 00:27:52,409
BUT I KEPT TRACK.

599
00:27:52,409 --> 00:27:54,150
I TRIED.

600
00:27:57,110 --> 00:27:59,068
AND LOOK AT HIM NOW.

601
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:02,942
LOOK AT MY BOY.

602
00:28:04,683 --> 00:28:08,077
HE WAS
A BRILLIANT YOUNG MAN.

603
00:28:08,077 --> 00:28:10,123
FROM NOTHING,
UNDER HIS OWN STEAM,

604
00:28:10,123 --> 00:28:13,343
HE GOT HIMSELF A SCHOLARSHIP
TO CAMBRIDGE TO STUDY CLASSICS.

605
00:28:13,343 --> 00:28:16,172
THAT'S WHAT GOT HIM INVITED

606
00:28:16,172 --> 00:28:19,132
TO PREVIEW
THE MUSEUM'S NEW COLLECTION.

607
00:28:19,132 --> 00:28:21,395
AND HE STOLE THE RING.

608
00:28:21,395 --> 00:28:24,180
[sighs]
THAT WAS AN IMPULSIVE ACT.

609
00:28:24,180 --> 00:28:25,791
HE'S NOT A THIEF.

610
00:28:25,791 --> 00:28:28,054
HE'S A FOOLISH,
REBELLIOUS KID.

611
00:28:28,054 --> 00:28:30,883
HE TOOK A COPY OF THE RING
IN WITH HIM.

612
00:28:30,883 --> 00:28:33,015
IT WASN'T AN IMPULSIVE ACT.
IT WAS A PLAN.

613
00:28:33,015 --> 00:28:35,452
HE'S NOT A THIEF.

614
00:28:35,452 --> 00:28:37,237
YOU BELIEVE THAT,

615
00:28:37,237 --> 00:28:39,239
AND THAT WAS YOUR PLAN.

616
00:28:39,239 --> 00:28:41,241
IF YOU COULD
JUST TALK TO HIM,

617
00:28:41,241 --> 00:28:43,243
HE'D RETURN THE RING,
BECAUSE HE'S...

618
00:28:43,243 --> 00:28:45,506
AS YOU SAY, NOT A THIEF.

619
00:28:45,506 --> 00:28:48,117
I COULD HAVE.

620
00:28:48,117 --> 00:28:51,642
IF I MADE IT IN TIME,
I COULD HAVE DONE THAT.

621
00:28:51,642 --> 00:28:54,820
AND NOW YOU TRACK DOWN
HIS KILLER

622
00:28:54,820 --> 00:28:56,560
AND KILL THEM.

623
00:28:56,560 --> 00:28:59,520
YEAH, WELL,
YOU KNOW HOW THAT WORKS.

624
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:01,565
I READ ALL ABOUT YOU,
MR. JANE.

625
00:29:01,565 --> 00:29:04,003
I KNOW WHAT HAPPENED.

626
00:29:09,835 --> 00:29:12,011
WELL,
YOU'LL END UP IN PRISON.

627
00:29:12,011 --> 00:29:14,404
MAYBE.

628
00:29:14,404 --> 00:29:17,016
BUT RIGHT NOW
I'M GONNA WALK OUT OF HERE,

629
00:29:17,016 --> 00:29:19,018
AND YOU'RE GONNA LET ME.

630
00:29:19,018 --> 00:29:21,063
OBVIOUSLY.
YOU'RE HOLDING A GUN,

631
00:29:21,063 --> 00:29:23,762
AND I HAVE NO REAL REASON
TO STOP YOU.

632
00:29:23,762 --> 00:29:25,807
THANKS FOR BEING SENSIBLE.

633
00:29:25,807 --> 00:29:28,679
IT'S MY MIDDLE NAME.

634
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:35,121
[Patrick clears throat]

635
00:29:35,121 --> 00:29:36,600
HEY.

636
00:29:36,600 --> 00:29:38,254
HEY.

637
00:29:38,254 --> 00:29:40,604
I'M HAVING A PRIVATE WORD
WITH EVERYONE HERE

638
00:29:40,604 --> 00:29:43,172
TO KINDA SET THE TONE.

639
00:29:43,172 --> 00:29:46,175
COOL. IT'S, UH,
AN EXCELLENT PRACTICE.

640
00:29:46,175 --> 00:29:47,524
HAVE A SEAT.

641
00:29:47,524 --> 00:29:49,135
THANK YOU.

642
00:29:49,135 --> 00:29:52,138
I SPOKE
TO LISBON YESTERDAY...MM-HMM.

643
00:29:52,138 --> 00:29:55,924
TOLD HER HOW DEEPLY I VALUE
YOUR CONTRIBUTION TO THE BUREAU.

644
00:29:57,796 --> 00:29:59,145
NICE TO HEAR.

645
00:29:59,145 --> 00:30:01,800
I TOLD HER YOU'RE TOO GOOD
TO LOSE

646
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:05,151
TO SOME SMART-ASS MOVE
YOU MIGHT MAKE THAT TURNS BAD.

647
00:30:05,151 --> 00:30:08,023
I TOLD HER THAT IF AND WHEN
IT HAPPENS, IT'S HER NECK.

648
00:30:10,025 --> 00:30:11,592
YOU...

649
00:30:11,592 --> 00:30:14,160
YOU'RE GOLDEN.

650
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:17,250
YOU'RE SAFE FOR ANYTHING
SHORT OF MURDER.

651
00:30:17,250 --> 00:30:20,644
LISBON--NO.

652
00:30:20,644 --> 00:30:23,169
YOU MESS UP,
SHE'S OUT OF HERE.

653
00:30:23,169 --> 00:30:25,040
ANY QUESTIONS?

654
00:30:25,040 --> 00:30:27,608
NOT THAT I CAN THINK OF
RIGHT NOW.

655
00:30:27,608 --> 00:30:30,045
GOOD.

656
00:30:30,045 --> 00:30:32,047
THANK YOU FOR YOUR TIME.

657
00:30:32,047 --> 00:30:34,920
I LOOK FORWARD
TO WORKING WITH YOU.

658
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:37,183
LIKEWISE.

659
00:30:37,183 --> 00:30:40,577
THANK YOU.

660
00:30:40,577 --> 00:30:42,623
SEE YOU AROUND.

661
00:30:46,627 --> 00:30:48,629
I KNEW THE PURCHASE WAS ILLEGAL.

662
00:30:48,629 --> 00:30:51,066
I JUST DIDN'T WANT TO GET IN TROUBLE.

663
00:30:51,066 --> 00:30:53,764
IRONIC. [chuckles]

664
00:30:53,764 --> 00:30:57,116
WHERE'S THE GUN NOW?I HAVE NO IDEA. I HAVEN'T
SEEN IT SINCE THE SHOOT,

665
00:30:57,116 --> 00:30:59,945
WHICH IS WHAT,
LIKE SIX WEEKS AGO?

666
00:30:59,945 --> 00:31:02,208
I THOUGHT IT MIGHT BE
SOMEWHERE IN MY STUDIO,

667
00:31:02,208 --> 00:31:05,864
BUT YOU GUYS WOULD HAVE
FOUND IT, I GUESS.

668
00:31:05,864 --> 00:31:08,040
MAYBE SOMEBODY STOLE IT.THAT'S NOT VERY CREDIBLE.

669
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:09,650
IT'S THE TRUTH.

670
00:31:09,650 --> 00:31:11,870
BOSS?YEAH.

671
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:14,698
I WAS GOING THROUGH THE FILES
ON BANKS' LAPTOP,

672
00:31:14,698 --> 00:31:17,658
AND I FOUND THIS AND THIS
IN HIS TELEPHONE RECORDS.

673
00:31:20,835 --> 00:31:23,838
CHO, YOU MIND?

674
00:31:23,838 --> 00:31:26,928
ALL YOURS.

675
00:31:26,928 --> 00:31:30,105
MR. BANKS, DO YOU KNOW ANYTHING
ABOUT THE THEFT OF A RING

676
00:31:30,105 --> 00:31:31,759
AT THE BRITISH MUSEUM?

677
00:31:31,759 --> 00:31:33,804
CLEOPATRA'S WEDDING RING,
SUPPOSEDLY.

678
00:31:33,804 --> 00:31:35,197
NO.

679
00:31:35,197 --> 00:31:36,982
WHY?

680
00:31:36,982 --> 00:31:40,289
WE CHECKED YOUR BROWSER HISTORY
ON YOUR OFFICE COMPUTER.

681
00:31:40,289 --> 00:31:43,336
YOU LOOKED UP THE THEFT
OF THE RING TWO MONTHS AGO,

682
00:31:43,336 --> 00:31:46,295
RIGHT AFTER YOU LET STANS
MOVE INTO YOUR POOL HOUSE.

683
00:31:46,295 --> 00:31:49,603
DOWNLOADED QUITE A BIT
ABOUT IT.

684
00:31:51,561 --> 00:31:53,389
I NEVER DID THIS.

685
00:31:53,389 --> 00:31:55,391
YOU ALSO MADE
SEVERAL PHONE CALLS

686
00:31:55,391 --> 00:31:57,393
TO A MAN NAMED LOUIS ANGLET,

687
00:31:57,393 --> 00:32:00,092
WHO WE BELIEVE MAY HAVE
PURCHASED THE RING.

688
00:32:00,092 --> 00:32:03,182
ANGLET?
I'VE NEVER HEARD OF HIM.

689
00:32:03,182 --> 00:32:05,793
THE CALLS ARE
IN YOUR PHONE RECORDS.

690
00:32:07,838 --> 00:32:10,145
I PAID FOR OVERNIGHT DELIVERY.

691
00:32:10,145 --> 00:32:13,018
I WAS TOLD GUARANTEED DELIVERY
BEFORE 10:00 A.M.

692
00:32:13,018 --> 00:32:15,063
AND IT'S NOT HERE YET.

693
00:32:15,063 --> 00:32:18,066
WELL, IF IT GETS HERE BY THEN
THAT'LL BE FINE. THANK YOU.

694
00:32:18,066 --> 00:32:21,113
NO WORD ON SLOCOMBE?NEVER DESPAIR.
VAN PELT BRINGS HOPE.

695
00:32:21,113 --> 00:32:24,246
UH, WE'VE BEEN TRACKING
THIS ANGLET GUY VIA CELL PHONE.

696
00:32:24,246 --> 00:32:26,596
OFF THAT, WE GOT A BEAD
ON HIS CREDIT CARD.

697
00:32:26,596 --> 00:32:29,643
THE THING IS, SOMEONE ELSE IS
TRACKING HIS PURCHASES AS WELL.

698
00:32:29,643 --> 00:32:31,471
HAS TO BE SLOCOMBE.

699
00:32:31,471 --> 00:32:34,256
AND AT 3:00 THIS AFTERNOON,
ANGLET HAS A MASSAGE BOOKED

700
00:32:34,256 --> 00:32:36,998
AT THE BLUE WILLOW SPA, RIGHT
HERE IN DOWNTOWN SACRAMENTO.

701
00:32:36,998 --> 00:32:38,957
MM-HMM. AND CHANCES ARE...

702
00:32:38,957 --> 00:32:40,436
SLOCOMBE WILL SHOW UP.

703
00:32:40,436 --> 00:32:43,352
SO GOOD.

704
00:32:51,230 --> 00:32:55,103
I GOT ANGLET.

705
00:32:55,103 --> 00:32:56,800
[sighs]

706
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:58,063
BOTTLE OF WATER, PLEASE.

707
00:33:03,590 --> 00:33:05,026
[lowered voice] I SEE SLOCOMBE.

708
00:33:05,026 --> 00:33:07,594
ANGLET?

709
00:33:07,594 --> 00:33:10,510
WHAT?GOT A QUESTION FOR YOU.

710
00:33:10,510 --> 00:33:14,079
OH, SORRY, I THINK YOU HAVE
THE WRONG GUY, BUT--HEY.DID YOU KILL MY BOY?

711
00:33:14,079 --> 00:33:16,168
NO.DID YOU KILL MY BOY?

712
00:33:16,168 --> 00:33:18,561
GET OFF ME![thud]

713
00:33:18,561 --> 00:33:22,000
[Rigsby] CBI! ON THE GROUND![Cho] SLOCOMBE!
SLOCOMBE, DROP THE WEAPON!

714
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:24,002
[crowd screams]DROP IT!

715
00:33:25,655 --> 00:33:26,961
[Slocombe grunts]

716
00:33:34,534 --> 00:33:37,406
I JUST MEANT TO QUESTION HIM.

717
00:33:37,406 --> 00:33:41,410
I DON'T KNOW WHAT CAME OVER ME.
I SAW RED.

718
00:33:41,410 --> 00:33:43,238
I'LL END UP IN PRISON,
JUST LIKE YOU PREDICTED.

719
00:33:43,238 --> 00:33:44,805
[scoffs] VERY FOOLISH.

720
00:33:44,805 --> 00:33:46,937
NO.

721
00:33:46,937 --> 00:33:48,635
IT'S HUMAN NATURE.

722
00:33:48,635 --> 00:33:51,464
AH, IT MADE ME REALIZE
REVENGE IS NOT FOR ME.

723
00:33:51,464 --> 00:33:53,857
POINTLESS. MORE VIOLENCE IS
JUST MORE VIOLENCE.

724
00:33:53,857 --> 00:33:55,859
DOESN'T MAKE ANYTHING
ANY BETTER.

725
00:33:55,859 --> 00:33:57,644
MM, MAYBE.

726
00:33:57,644 --> 00:33:59,602
I'M NOT SO, UH...

727
00:33:59,602 --> 00:34:03,171
YOU'RE BOOKED ON THE 8:00
TO LONDON TOMORROW MORNING.

728
00:34:03,171 --> 00:34:06,392
TAKE IT, AND THERE'LL BE
NO CHARGES PENDING.THANK YOU.

729
00:34:06,392 --> 00:34:08,698
I DON'T WANT TO SEE YOU AGAIN.
CLEAR?

730
00:34:08,698 --> 00:34:10,787
OH, YES, MA'AM.

731
00:34:10,787 --> 00:34:12,398
THANK YOU.

732
00:34:16,576 --> 00:34:19,144
UH, TH-THAT'S MINE.

733
00:34:21,581 --> 00:34:23,017
YEP.[pen clicks]

734
00:34:29,545 --> 00:34:32,461
FRANCIS SLOCOMBE, THE MAN
WHO WAS TRYING TO KILL YOU--

735
00:34:32,461 --> 00:34:33,810
WHY WAS THAT?

736
00:34:33,810 --> 00:34:36,422
I HAVE NO IDEA.

737
00:34:36,422 --> 00:34:38,641
WE KNOW THAT SLOCOMBE WAS TRACKING YOU.

738
00:34:38,641 --> 00:34:41,079
WE KNOW THAT YOU CAME HERE FOR THE RING.

739
00:34:41,079 --> 00:34:43,516
THIS RING MUST BE
VERY IMPORTANT.

740
00:34:43,516 --> 00:34:47,128
ANGLET'S LAWYER'S HERE. EVERYONE HERE SEEMS
TO BE TALKING ABOUT IT.

741
00:34:47,128 --> 00:34:50,566
WHAT KIND OF RING IS IT?AGENT LISBON.

742
00:34:50,566 --> 00:34:52,351
EXCUSE ME.

743
00:34:55,876 --> 00:34:58,705
[whistles and inhales sharply]

744
00:34:58,705 --> 00:35:01,882
HE'S TOUGH.YEAH, WELL, THERE'S A REASON
WHY HE HASN'T BEEN IN JAIL.

745
00:35:01,882 --> 00:35:03,536
THAT'S HIS ATTORNEY.

746
00:35:03,536 --> 00:35:05,581
PROBABLY GETS ABOUT
$1,500 AN HOUR.

747
00:35:05,581 --> 00:35:08,541
LET'S SPEND A LITTLE TIME
WITH HIM, RUN UP THE METER.

748
00:35:13,241 --> 00:35:15,243
EXCUSE ME.
I'M AGENT LISBON.

749
00:35:15,243 --> 00:35:18,681
WOULD YOU COME TO MY OFFICE
WITH ME, PLEASE? JUST UP HERE.

750
00:35:30,693 --> 00:35:32,173
HI.

751
00:35:32,173 --> 00:35:36,308
WHOA. YOU DON'T LOOK LIKE
MY LAWYER.

752
00:35:36,308 --> 00:35:39,180
I'LL TAKE THAT
AS A COMPLIMENT.I'M NOT GONNA ANSWER
ANY MORE QUESTIONS.

753
00:35:39,180 --> 00:35:41,051
NO MORE QUESTIONS.

754
00:35:41,051 --> 00:35:44,054
I KNOW YOU DIDN'T KILL STANS.
YOU'RE TOO SMART FOR THAT.

755
00:35:44,054 --> 00:35:47,057
BUT WHAT YOU DID DO IS YOU
BOUGHT CLEOPATRA'S WEDDING RING

756
00:35:47,057 --> 00:35:49,147
FROM HIS KILLER.OH, THECLEOPATRA?

757
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:52,454
REALLY? QUEEN OF THE NILE,
THE BRIDE OF MARK ANTONY?

758
00:35:52,454 --> 00:35:55,457
[increases volume] AND HERE'S WHAT YOU GOT--

759
00:35:55,457 --> 00:35:56,937
ONE OF THESE...

760
00:35:56,937 --> 00:35:59,635
$39 FAKIES.

761
00:35:59,635 --> 00:36:03,117
CONSIDERABLY MORE IF YOU HAVE TO GET THE OVERNIGHT DELIVERY.

762
00:36:03,117 --> 00:36:04,553
NOT YOUR FAULT.

763
00:36:04,553 --> 00:36:07,513
NO REASON TO THINK
IT WAS A FAKE, OBVIOUSLY.

764
00:36:07,513 --> 00:36:09,689
STANS DID STEAL THE RING.

765
00:36:09,689 --> 00:36:11,691
THAT'S WHY
IT'S SUCH A GREAT SCAM.

766
00:36:11,691 --> 00:36:15,564
HE CAN SELL THE SAME RING
OVER AND OVER.

767
00:36:15,564 --> 00:36:18,654
NOW THE PERSON YOU BOUGHT
THE RING FOR--

768
00:36:18,654 --> 00:36:22,658
I'M GUESSING THEY PAID MORE
THAN $39 FOR IT.

769
00:36:22,658 --> 00:36:25,661
HOW MUCH DID THEY PAY FOR IT?
HUH?

770
00:36:25,661 --> 00:36:28,621
$200,000?

771
00:36:30,536 --> 00:36:32,886
MORE?

772
00:36:32,886 --> 00:36:34,975
MORE THAN $200,000?

773
00:36:34,975 --> 00:36:36,977
OHH.

774
00:36:36,977 --> 00:36:38,979
I THINK
THEY'RE GONNA BE PRETTY MAD

775
00:36:38,979 --> 00:36:41,329
WHEN THEY FIND OUT
IT'S A FAKE.

776
00:36:41,329 --> 00:36:44,463
OHH! WHAT DO YOU THINK?

777
00:36:44,463 --> 00:36:46,682
[laughs] OH, MAN.

778
00:36:46,682 --> 00:36:50,077
YOU CAN GO NOW, MR. ANGLET.
YOUR ATTORNEY'S WAITING.

779
00:36:53,167 --> 00:36:54,516
SEE YOU.

780
00:36:57,867 --> 00:36:59,608
YOU STAY.

781
00:36:59,608 --> 00:37:01,001
OH, I'M STAYING.

782
00:37:01,001 --> 00:37:03,830
THE PHONE
AND INTERNET EVIDENCE SUGGESTS

783
00:37:03,830 --> 00:37:07,921
THAT HOPPER KILLED STANS FOR
THE RING AND SOLD IT TO ANGLET.YES, IT DOES SUGGEST THAT.

784
00:37:07,921 --> 00:37:10,706
SO YOU JUST PUT HOPPER
IN A GREAT DEAL OF DANGER.

785
00:37:10,706 --> 00:37:13,622
[whispers] NAH.

786
00:37:13,622 --> 00:37:15,276
[whispers] NAH?

787
00:37:15,276 --> 00:37:17,235
[normal voice]
THAT'S YOUR CONSIDERED REPLY?

788
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:19,672
YEP.

789
00:37:19,672 --> 00:37:22,675
PUT A GUARD ON HOPPER ASAP.WILL DO, BOSS.

790
00:37:22,675 --> 00:37:25,025
YOU KNOW, THIS IS EXACTLY

791
00:37:25,025 --> 00:37:27,549
THE KIND OF SCENARIO
WE TALKED ABOUT.HMM.

792
00:37:27,549 --> 00:37:30,248
DIDN'T THINK
WE'D GET THERE SO SOON.

793
00:37:31,771 --> 00:37:34,252
YOU BUTT IS ON THE LINE,
AGENT LISBON.

794
00:37:39,648 --> 00:37:41,389
WHAT DID YOU DO?

795
00:37:41,389 --> 00:37:44,174
PAID WAY TOO MUCH
FOR OVERNIGHT DELIVERY.

796
00:37:44,174 --> 00:37:46,351
MAYBE WE SHOULD CONSIDER...

797
00:37:46,351 --> 00:37:50,137
PROTECTIVE CUSTODY?
NO. NO WAY.I'LL PUT A TEAM TOGETHER, SIR.

798
00:37:50,137 --> 00:37:53,227
FULL PROTECTION 24/7,
MY 4 BEST GUYS.

799
00:37:53,227 --> 00:37:56,143
MR. BANKS,
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND--SURE, I DO. YOU PEOPLE CONVINCED
ANGLET THAT I CHEATED HIM,

800
00:37:56,143 --> 00:37:58,580
AND THEN TURNED HIM LOOSE
TO KILL ME.

801
00:37:58,580 --> 00:38:01,409
THAT PRETTY MUCH HOW IT GOES?YEAH, THAT'S--THAT'S
PRETTY MUCH HOW IT GOES.

802
00:38:01,409 --> 00:38:03,324
BUT FOR THE RECORD,

803
00:38:03,324 --> 00:38:06,458
AGENT LISBON HAD ABSOLUTELY
NOTHING TO DO WITH THIS.JANE--

804
00:38:06,458 --> 00:38:09,374
HOW GALLANT.IT WAS ALL MY IDEA.
A-AND WE COULD HAVE HELD ANGLET

805
00:38:09,374 --> 00:38:11,419
IF YOU WERE MAN ENOUGH
TO ADMIT

806
00:38:11,419 --> 00:38:14,596
SELLING HIM THE RING
IN THE FIRST PLACE.THAT'S IT. GET OUT.

807
00:38:14,596 --> 00:38:16,729
YOU BETTER PRAY
NOTHING HAPPENS TO MY FAMILY.

808
00:38:28,523 --> 00:38:30,612
[engine sputters]

809
00:38:30,612 --> 00:38:32,222
OH, COME ON.

810
00:38:37,924 --> 00:38:40,883
[grunts][grunts]

811
00:38:40,883 --> 00:38:43,756
[both grunting]

812
00:38:45,410 --> 00:38:47,890
WHERE IS IT?

813
00:38:47,890 --> 00:38:50,110
I WANT THE REAL RING NOW.

814
00:38:50,110 --> 00:38:52,939
[panting] WHAT ARE YOU TALKING
ABOUT? I GAVE IT TO YOU.

815
00:38:52,939 --> 00:38:54,941
YOU SOLD ME THE FAKE.

816
00:38:54,941 --> 00:38:57,073
I WANT THE REAL ONE NOW.

817
00:38:57,073 --> 00:38:59,598
I... I GAVE YOU THE REAL ONE,
ALL RIGHT?

818
00:38:59,598 --> 00:39:02,557
TRUST ME. I PUT A GUN
IN THAT GUY'S FACE.

819
00:39:02,557 --> 00:39:04,646
THERE'S NO WAY
HE'D HAND OVER A FAKE.

820
00:39:04,646 --> 00:39:06,866
[sirens wail][Lisbon] PUT THE GUN DOWN!

821
00:39:06,866 --> 00:39:10,435
[Rigsby] DROP THE GUN!ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.
HEY, WHAT DID I DO?

822
00:39:10,435 --> 00:39:13,699
I JUST HELPED YOU CATCH
THE GUY. ALL RIGHT, RELAX.ON THE GROUND!

823
00:39:13,699 --> 00:39:16,702
[Van Pelt] PUT YOUR HANDS
ON YOUR HEAD.LET'S SEE YOUR HANDS.
UP AGAINST THE TRUCK, BANDINO.

824
00:39:16,702 --> 00:39:19,531
GO! GO!
LET'S SEE YOUR HANDS.

825
00:39:20,967 --> 00:39:22,708
VICTOR BANDINO,

826
00:39:22,708 --> 00:39:25,624
YOU'RE UNDER ARREST
FOR THE MURDER OF OLIVER STANS.

827
00:39:28,757 --> 00:39:31,194
YEAH, YOU THINK
BEING A COP'S STRESSFUL?

828
00:39:31,194 --> 00:39:33,283
TRY BEING A COP IN PRISON,
JERK.

829
00:39:33,283 --> 00:39:35,808
[police radio chatter]

830
00:39:38,463 --> 00:39:39,899
I KNOW MY JOB.

831
00:39:39,899 --> 00:39:42,292
I DO GOOD BACKGROUND CHECKS.

832
00:39:42,292 --> 00:39:45,208
I FOUND OUT THAT SMITHSON
WAS REALLY STANS,

833
00:39:45,208 --> 00:39:47,254
FOUND OUT ABOUT THE RING.

834
00:39:47,254 --> 00:39:49,256
I APPROACHED HIM.
WE TALKED.

835
00:39:49,256 --> 00:39:51,650
HE COULDN'T SELL THE RING.
IT WAS TOO HOT.

836
00:39:51,650 --> 00:39:54,261
BUT I KNOW SOME PEOPLE
WHO KNOW SOME PEOPLE

837
00:39:54,261 --> 00:39:57,220
THAT PUT ME IN TOUCH
WITH ANGLET, AND THAT WAS IT.

838
00:39:57,220 --> 00:39:58,744
I BROKERED THE DEAL.

839
00:39:58,744 --> 00:40:01,355
WHY'D YOU KILL STANS?

840
00:40:01,355 --> 00:40:04,489
HE CHANGED HIS MIND.

841
00:40:04,489 --> 00:40:06,621
DIDN'T WANT TO SELL IT.

842
00:40:06,621 --> 00:40:10,190
AT THE LAST MINUTE,
THE IDIOT WANTED TO CONFESS,

843
00:40:10,190 --> 00:40:12,235
RETURN IT TO THE MUSEUM.

844
00:40:12,235 --> 00:40:14,237
WHAT WAS I SUPPOSED TO DO?

845
00:40:14,237 --> 00:40:16,065
YOU SHOT HIM.

846
00:40:18,938 --> 00:40:20,548
I HAD NO CHOICE.

847
00:40:20,548 --> 00:40:23,246
IT WAS
A SPUR OF THE MOMENT THING.

848
00:40:23,246 --> 00:40:26,467
RIGHT. NO PREMEDITATION,
NO DEATH PENALTY.

849
00:40:26,467 --> 00:40:29,252
THE ONLY THING?
YOU PLANNED AHEAD.

850
00:40:29,252 --> 00:40:31,646
YOU PLANTED THE PHONE
AND INTERNET EVIDENCE

851
00:40:31,646 --> 00:40:34,649
ON HOPPER BANKS.
THAT DOESN'T LOOK GOOD.

852
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:44,050
BYE, SON.

853
00:40:46,835 --> 00:40:48,620
OKAY.

854
00:41:06,768 --> 00:41:09,858
WELL, IT APPEARS I WAS...
WRONG ABOUT YOUR SON.

855
00:41:09,858 --> 00:41:13,558
HE WASN'T A THIEF.
HE WANTED TO RETURN THE RING.

856
00:41:13,558 --> 00:41:16,778
ANGLET CUT A DEAL,

857
00:41:16,778 --> 00:41:18,650
TRADED FOR HIS FREEDOM.

858
00:41:18,650 --> 00:41:20,826
WAY OF THE WORLD.

859
00:41:20,826 --> 00:41:23,263
YEAH. IT DOESN'T FEEL
ANY BETTER.

860
00:41:23,263 --> 00:41:25,787
KNOWING WHO KILLED HIM,
KNOWING HE'LL BE PUNISHED--

861
00:41:25,787 --> 00:41:27,920
IT DOESN'T MAKE
A DAMN BIT OF DIFFERENCE.

862
00:41:27,920 --> 00:41:30,313
I THOUGHT IT WOULD.

863
00:41:30,313 --> 00:41:31,924
BUT THIS...

864
00:41:31,924 --> 00:41:34,535
IS WHAT HE WANTED.

865
00:41:34,535 --> 00:41:37,059
I CAN GIVE THAT TO HIM NOW,
THANKS TO YOU.

866
00:41:37,059 --> 00:41:38,974
EH.

867
00:41:38,974 --> 00:41:41,586
WELL,

868
00:41:41,586 --> 00:41:43,588
I BETTER NOT MISS MY PLANE.

869
00:41:43,588 --> 00:41:45,590
TIME TO SAY GOOD-BYE.

870
00:41:45,590 --> 00:41:47,940
YEAH. GOOD-BYE.

871
00:41:47,940 --> 00:41:50,638
I WASN'T GONNA HUG YOU.

872
00:41:50,638 --> 00:41:52,597
I KNOW. JUST MAKING SURE.

873
00:41:54,729 --> 00:41:59,691
[Lisbon] OH, NO.[Patrick] THERE WAS
A CERTAIN VULNERABILITY,

874
00:41:59,691 --> 00:42:01,823
A CERTAIN RUMPLED GENTLENESS
TO HIM.

875
00:42:01,823 --> 00:42:04,347
VULNERABILITY?

876
00:42:04,347 --> 00:42:06,611
MM, I THOUGHT SO.

877
00:42:06,611 --> 00:42:09,439
YEAH.

878
00:42:09,439 --> 00:42:12,007
COMFORTABLE?

879
00:42:12,007 --> 00:42:14,270
I'M GETTING THERE, YEAH.

880
00:42:17,143 --> 00:42:19,580
REGARDING
AGENTS RIGSBY AND VAN PELT--

881
00:42:19,580 --> 00:42:22,583
THEY'RE
IN A ROMANTIC RELATIONSHIP.

882
00:42:22,583 --> 00:42:25,368
WELL, I...
WELL, ROMANTIC?

883
00:42:25,368 --> 00:42:28,371
YOU'RE TOO GOOD OF A COP
NOT TO HAVE NOTICED,

884
00:42:28,371 --> 00:42:30,939
AND SINCE YOU HAVEN'T DONE
ANYTHING ABOUT IT,

885
00:42:30,939 --> 00:42:32,941
I'M GONNA HAVE TO
TAKE ACTION MYSELF.

886
00:42:32,941 --> 00:42:36,205
JUST WANTED
TO LET YOU KNOW FIRST.

887
00:42:36,205 --> 00:42:38,338
GOOD NIGHT.

888
00:42:38,338 --> 00:42:40,122
GOOD NIGHT.

889
00:42:50,611 --> 00:42:52,265
SHE'S GOOD.

890
00:42:58,750 --> 00:43:01,535
STAY TUNED FOR SCENES
FROM OUR NEXT EPISODE.

